DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbtthhiiddccoonnttrrooll utility can be used to query remote Bluetooth HID de‐
     vices, dump HID descriptors in human readable form and perform simple ma‐
     nipulations on the Bluetooth HID daemon configuration files.

     The bbtthhiiddccoonnttrrooll utility will print results to the standard output and
     error messages to the standard error.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa _B_D___A_D_D_R
             Specify BD_ADDR for the HID device.  Example: --aa
             00:01:02:03:04:05.

     --cc _f_i_l_e
             Specify path to the Bluetooth HID daemon configuration file.  The
             default path is _/_e_t_c_/_b_l_u_e_t_o_o_t_h_/_b_t_h_i_d_d_._c_o_n_f.

     --HH _f_i_l_e
             Specify path to the Bluetooth HID daemon known HIDs file.  The
             default path is _/_v_a_r_/_d_b_/_b_t_h_i_d_d_._h_i_d_s.

     --hh      Display usage message and exit.

     --vv      Be verbose and show items that are being used for padding.

     _c_o_m_m_a_n_d
             One of the supported commands (see below).  Special command hheellpp
             can be used to obtain the list of all supported commands.  To get
             more information about specific command use hheellpp _c_o_m_m_a_n_d.

